="2.1"/><path d="M12 13v1.3"/></svg></span><span><b>Uranus</b><small class="is-on"><span class="today-hide-m">Retrograde · </span>Sep 10 to Feb 8, 2027</small></span></div><div class="today-rt__track" role="cell"><span class="sr-only">Retrograde now</span><i class="today-rt__bar is-now" style="left:16.78%;width:62.03%"></i></div></div><div class="today-rt__row" role="row"><div class="today-rt__name" role="rowheader"><span class="today-rt__g" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6.5 5.6v4.2M17.5 5.6v4.2M12 4.4V20"/><path d="M6.5 9.8a6 6 0 0 0 11 0"/><path d="M9 16.6h6"/></svg></span><span><b>Neptune</b><small class="is-on"><span class="today-hide-m">Retrograde · </span>Jul 7 to Dec 12</small></span></div><div class="today-rt__track" role="cell"><span class="sr-only">Retrograde now</span><i class="today-rt__bar is-now is-clip-start" style="left:0%;width:55.12%"></i></div></div><div class="today-rt__row" role="row"><div class="today-rt__name" role="rowheader"><span class="today-rt__g" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7 8.8a5 5 0 0 0 10 0"/><circle cx="12" cy="6.6" r="2.2"/><path d="M12 13.6v7M9 17.1h6"/></svg></span><span><b>Pluto</b><small>May 6 to Oct 16, now direct</small></span></div><div class="today-rt__track" role="cell"><span class="sr-only">Ended</span><i class="today-rt__bar is-ended is-clip-start" style="left:0%;width:31.32%"></i></div></div></div><div class="today-rt__key" aria-hidden="true"><span><i></i>Retrograde now</span><span><i class="is-upcoming"></i>Coming up</span><span><i class="is-ended"></i>Ended</span><span><i class="is-today"></i><span><span data-edition-current-only>Today, </span>Nov 5</span></span></div><div class="today-note"><span class="kicker">What retrograde means</span><p>Seen from Earth, a planet sometimes appears to slow, stop and drift backward against the stars. Nothing changes in its real orbit. Astrologers have long read these stretches as a time for review: the planet’s themes are revisited rather than begun.</p></div></section><!-- 7. The closest angles in this sky, each with what it has
+          traditionally been read as. --><section class="kwrap today-sec" aria-labelledby="today-aspects-heading"><div class="section-head--row today-head"><div><h2 id="today-aspects-heading" class="h-2">Today’s closest aspects</h2><p>Aspects are the angles between planets. Five are within three degrees of exact at noon UTC; these are the four closest.</p></div><a class="textlink only-desktop" href="/learn/aspects/">How aspects work <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="today-asps"><article class="kcard today-asp"><div class="today-asp__g" aria-hidden="true"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="8.4" r="4.4"/><path d="M12 12.8v8.2M8.6 17.4h6.8"/></svg></span><svg class="today-asp__type is-sextile" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 4.5v15M5.5 8.25l13 7.5M18.5 8.25l-13 7.5"/></svg><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7.6 10.2c0-4.2 6.2-4.2 6.2 0v9.6"/><path d="M9.3 16.3h6.6"/></svg></span></div><h3 class="h-4">Venus sextile Jupiter</h3><p class="today-asp__pos">24°20′ Libra Rx · 24°50′ Leo</p><p>A 60° aspect read as an opportunity for two parts of the chart to cooperate. Venus has traditionally stood for affection, pleasure, and values, Jupiter for growth and belief.</p><span class="today-asp__tag">0°30′ from exact</span></article><article class="kcard today-asp"><div class="today-asp__g" aria-hidden="true"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6.5 5.6v4.2M17.5 5.6v4.2M12 4.4V20"/><path d="M6.5 9.8a6 6 0 0 0 11 0"/><path d="M9 16.6h6"/></svg></span><svg class="today-asp__type is-sextile" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 4.5v15M5.5 8.25l13 7.5M18.5 8.25l-13 7.5"/></svg><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7 8.8a5 5 0 0 0 10 0"/><circle cx="12" cy="6.6" r="2.2"/><path d="M12 13.6v7M9 17.1h6"/></svg></span></div><h3 class="h-4">Neptune sextile Pluto</h3><p class="today-asp__pos">1°59′ Aries Rx · 3°10′ Aquarius</p><p>A 60° aspect read as an opportunity for two parts of the chart to cooperate. Neptune has traditionally stood for imagination and ideals, Pluto for power and deep change.</p><span class="today-asp__tag">1°10′ from exact</span></article><article class="kcard today-asp"><div class="today-asp__g" aria-hidden="true"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M8 6v7M16 6v7M8 9.4h8M12 6v6.4"/><circle cx="12" cy="16.4" r="2.1"/><path d="M12 13v1.3"/></svg></span><svg class="today-asp__type is-trine" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5.4 19 18.2H5Z"/></svg><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7 8.8a5 5 0 0 0 10 0"/><circle cx="12" cy="6.6" r="2.2"/><path d="M12 13.6v7M9 17.1h6"/></svg></span></div><h3 class="h-4">Uranus trine Pluto</h3><p class="today-asp__pos">4°30′ Gemini Rx · 3°10′ Aquarius</p><p>A 120° aspect read as an easy-flowing connection between two parts of the chart. Uranus has traditionally stood for independence and change, Pluto for power and deep change.</p><span class="today-asp__tag">1°20′ from exact</span></article><article class="kcard today-asp"><div class="today-asp__g" aria-hidden="true"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="7.4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.5" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></span><svg class="today-asp__type is-conjunction" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="10.4" cy="13.6" r="4"/><path d="M13.2 10.8 18.4 5.6"/></svg><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M8.7 4.6a3.3 3.3 0 0 0 6.6 0"/><circle cx="12" cy="10.4" r="3.2"/><path d="M12 13.6v6M9 16.6h6"/></svg></span></div><h3 class="h-4">Sun conjunction Mercury</h3><p class="today-asp__pos">13°04′ Scorpio · 11°00′ Scorpio Rx</p><p>A 0° aspect that concentrates two parts of the chart in the same place. The Sun has traditionally stood for identity and direction, Mercury for thinking and communication.</p><span class="today-asp__tag">2°03′ from exact</span></article></div></section><!-- 8. Go further, and questions for Guide. --><section class="kwrap today-sec" aria-labelledby="today-further-heading"><div class="section-head--row today-head"><div><h2 id="today-further-heading" class="h-2">Go further</h2><p>More ways to follow the sky, date by date.</p></div><a class="textlink only-desktop" href="/tools/">All tools <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="grid-4 today-tools"><a class="kcard today-tool" href="/transits/"><span class="tool-icon" style="--tool-icon-hue:var(--sign-sagittarius);--tool-icon-box:48px" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-k4aetswt><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-astro-cid-k4aetswt><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.3" stroke-dasharray="2.3 2.5"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.6"/><circle cx="17.9" cy="6.1" r="2" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></span><h3 class="h-4">Transit tracker</h3><p>Today’s planets against your own chart.</p><span class="kcard__go" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="kcard today-tool" href="/moon-phase/"><span class="tool-icon" style="--tool-icon-hue:var(--sign-cancer);--tool-icon-box:48px" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-k4aetswt><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-astro-cid-k4aetswt><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.3"/><path d="M12 3.7a4.3 8.3 0 0 1 0 16.6"/></svg></span><h3 class="h-4">Moon phase</h3><p>Tonight’s moon, or the moon on any date.</p><span class="kcard__go" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="kcard today-tool" href="/sky-calendar/"><span class="tool-icon" style="--tool-icon-hue:var(--sign-taurus);--tool-icon-box:48px" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-k4aetswt><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-astro-cid-k4aetswt><rect x="4.2" y="5.6" width="15.6" height="14.4" rx="2.2"/><path d="M4.2 9.6h15.6M8.6 3.6v3.6M15.4 3.6v3.6"/><path d="M12 11.9C12.32 13.99 12.81 14.48 14.9 14.8C12.81 15.12 12.32 15.61 12 17.7C11.68 15.61 11.19 15.12 9.1 14.8C11.19 14.48 11.68 13.99 12 11.9Z"/></svg></span><h3 class="h-4">Sky calendar</h3><p>New and full moons in your calendar app.</p><span class="kcard__go" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="kcard today-tool" href="/eclipses/"><span class="tool-icon" style="--tool-icon-hue:var(--sign-scorpio);--tool-icon-box:48px" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-k4aetswt><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-astro-cid-k4aetswt><circle cx="9.8" cy="9.8" r="5.4"/><path d="M3.3 9.8H2.6M9.8 3.3v-.7M5.2 5.2l-.5-.5"/><circle cx="14.2" cy="14.2" r="5.4" style="fill:var(--tool-icon-hue)"/></svg></span><h3 class="h-4">Eclipses</h3><p>Solar and lunar eclipses through 2028.</p><span class="kcard__go" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="kcard kcard--raised today-ask"><div><h3 class="h-4">Questions about today’s sky?</h3><p class="ask-guide-line" data-astro-cid-fzv6vkti>Guide is an AI assistant for astrology questions and help using Zodiacs. <a href="/ask/" data-assistant-open data-assistant-locale="en" data-astro-cid-fzv6vkti>Ask Guide</a></p></div><nav class="guide-prompts" aria-label="Ask Guide" data-astro-cid-ehht7mum><ul class="guide-prompts__list" data-astro-cid-ehht7mum><li data-astro-cid-ehht7mum><a class="guide-prompts__chip" href="/ask/" data-assistant-open data-assistant-locale="en" data-assistant-prompt="What does today’s sky mean for my sign?" data-astro-cid-ehht7mum>What does today’s sky mean for my sign?</a></li><li data-astro-cid-ehht7mum><a class="guide-prompts__chip" href="/ask/" data-assistant-open data-assistant-locale="en" data-assistant-prompt="What is a retrograde?" data-astro-cid-ehht7mum>What is a retrograde?</a></li><li data-astro-cid-ehht7mum><a class="guide-prompts__chip" href="/ask/" data-assistant-open data-assistant-locale="en" data-assistant-prompt="How do I read today’s sky against my birth chart?" data-astro-cid-ehht7mum>How do I read today’s sky against my birth chart?</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><!-- 9. How the page is made. --><section class="kwrap today-method" aria-labelledby="today-method-heading"><h2 id="today-method-heading" class="h-4">How this page is made</h2><div><p>Positions are calculated for noon UTC on the edition date, November 5, 2026. Calendar times are UTC. The sign notes describe themes for reflection, not advice.</p><details class="evidence-disclosure evidence-disclosure--quiet today-provenance" data-evidence-disclosure data-evidence-variant="quiet"><summary><span class="evidence-disclosure__summary"><strong>Behind this daily reading</strong><small>Sky details, limitations, and editorial standards</small></span></summary><div class="evidence-disclosure__body"><p>Each reading is tied to the recorded sky for <time datetime="2026-11-05">2026-11-05</time>, the UTC edition date; planetary positions use a noon-UTC snapshot. Automated checks verify the sky facts, keep the twelve signs meaningfully distinct, and screen restricted advice before an edition is published.</p></div></details><p class="today-method__links"><a class="textlink" href="/methodology/#daily-publication">How daily publication works <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="textlink" href="/data/daily-publication.json">This edition’s record <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="textlink" href="/corrections/">Corrections <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></section></section></main><footer class="zfooter"><div class="zfooter__inner"><section class="email-capture email-capture--footer" data-email-capture-shell data-placement="footer" data-daily-capture="true" aria-labelledby="email-footer-en-title" data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4><div class="email-capture__copy" data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4><h2 id="email-footer-en-title" data-email-title data-default-title="The daily, by email." data-personal-title="Your {sign} day ahead." data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4>The daily, by email.</h2><p data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4>Your sign’s reading each morning. Free, unsubscribe anytime.</p></div><form class="email-capture__form" method="post" action="/api/email/subscribe" data-email-capture data-placement="footer" data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4><input type="hidden" name="locale" value="en" data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4><div class="email-capture__trap" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4><label for="email-footer-en-website" data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4>Leave this field blank</label><input id="email-footer-en-website" name="website" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4></div><div class="email-capture__email-row" data-astro-cid-i26ydgg4><div cl